[36m(TaskRunner pid=2771338)[0m [text][response] <reasoning>
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2771338)[0m I need to make Venmo requests to my roommates for their share of Amazon orders. First, I need to retrieve the Amazon order details to calculate each roommate's share. 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2771338)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2771338)[0m The amazon__show_orders API requires an access token, which I can obtain by logging in to Amazon using the password retrieved from supervisor__show_account_passwords. The password for amazon is "]KpCzej" (note the closing quote).
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2771338)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2771338)[0m After retrieving the orders, I need to identify all roommates. These would be contacts in the phone contacts application. I'll search contacts and identify the roommate contacts.
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2771338)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2771338)[0m Then I'll calculate the total cost and divide it equally among all roommates. For each roommate, I'll create a Venmo transaction with the calculated amount and description "For Amazon Orders".
